<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Hardie buys Boral Gypsum.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Hardie buys Boral Gypsum.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>James Hardie Industries Ltd said on Friday it had acquired Boral Ltd's U.S. plasterboard operation, Briar Gypsum, for A$121 million.  </p>
<p>James Hardie also announced a A$10 million expansion of its gypsum plant in Las Vegas, complementing the A$35 million expansion at its Seattle gypsum plant, currently underway.</p>
<p>Hardie said the initiatives would transform the company into the United States' fourth largest gypsum plasterboard producer, with total capacity equivalent to 7.5 percent of U.S. gypsum production.</p>
<p>Production capacity would almost triple from 770 milion square feet to 1,985 million square feet, and sales revenue from the gypsum business would more than double to above A$200 million.</p>
